        "original_id": "2119cb08-0f2c-54bf-96c1-672c93b42172",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chas Chandler, John Constantine, Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, John Totleben, Jamie Delano, Philip Bond\n- Companies: DC Comics, Vertigo\n- Products: John Constantine, Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood, Northlanders\n- Roles: sidekick, cab driver, antihero\n\nFacts:\n- John Constantine debuted in comic books in 1984 in Swamp Thing No. 25, dated June 1984.\n- Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, and John Totleben created John Constantine.\n- John Constantine is a fictional antihero who appears in comic books published by DC Comics and its alternative imprint Vertigo.\n- Chas Chandler is John Constantine's closest and longest surviving friend, and he acts as Constantine's sidekick and cab driver.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood was written by Jamie Delano and illustrated by Philip Bond.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood features John Constantine several decades after most of his series continuity.\n- Northlanders is an American comic book series published by DC Comics under its Vertigo imprint.",
